@startuml
title Iteration 4 - Swarm Dispatch & Fault Recovery

participant "FireIncident" as FIS
participant "Scheduler\n(Port 5000)" as SCH
participant "SimulatorGUI" as GUI
participant "Drone 1" as D1
participant "Drone 2" as D2

== Normal Dispatch ==
FIS -[#blue]> SCH : UDP [FIRE:3:HIGH:NONE]
SCH -[#blue]> D1 : UDP [CMD:3:HIGH:NONE]
D1 -[#blue]> SCH : UDP [STATUS:1:EN_ROUTE:3:150:200:NONE]
SCH -> GUI : updateDronePosition(1)

== Hard Fault: Nozzle Jammed ==
FIS -[#blue]> SCH : UDP [FIRE:5:HIGH:NOZZLE_JAMMED]
SCH -[#blue]> D1 : UDP [CMD:5:HIGH:NOZZLE_JAMMED]
D1 -[#blue]> SCH : UDP [STATUS:1:HARD_FAULT:5:300:400:NOZZLE_JAMMED]

SCH -> GUI : markDroneFault(1, NOZZLE_JAMMED)
note right of SCH
  Drone 1 marked permanently offline.
  Mission 5 stripped of fault and re-queued.
end note

SCH -[#blue]> D2 : UDP [CMD:5:HIGH:NONE]

== Soft Fault: Packet Loss (Watchdog) ==
FIS -[#blue]> SCH : UDP [FIRE:4:LOW:PACKET_LOSS]
SCH -[#blue]> D2 : UDP [CMD:4:LOW:PACKET_LOSS]

note right of D2 : Drone flies but drops STATUS packets
... 30 seconds elapse with no UDP STATUS ...

SCH -> GUI : markDroneFault(2, PACKET_LOSS)
note right of SCH
  Watchdog triggers.
  Mission 4 stripped of fault and re-queued.
end note

SCH -[#blue]> D1 : UDP [CMD:4:LOW:NONE]

@enduml